{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>And he mentioned the Festival of Unleavened Bread.</b> As it was mentioned in the preceding section, because he mentioned that on it you went out from Egypt, and behold the Festival of Unleavened Bread is a remembrance, he mentioned the matter of the firstborn of a donkey, which is also a remembrance of the exodus from Egypt, as in the verse \"and when you reap\" (Leviticus 23:22), which he mentioned along with the Festival of Harvest, and likewise he mentioned this in the section \"You shall be holy,\" and on account of this, every firstborn is Mine:"], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:40:19.803714167Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}